{% doc %}
  DEMO SCAFFOLDING — maps a product handle to stand-in photography.

  The Redkisses demo store is on a Shopify trial plan, and Shopify blocks all
  product media uploads on trial accounts ("The file is not supported on trial
  accounts"). So the demo products have no images of their own. This snippet
  supplies stand-in photos so the storefront can be demoed with real imagery.

  It is a FALLBACK ONLY: every caller checks the product's own media first, so
  the moment the store is upgraded and real images are uploaded, these stop
  being used with no theme change. Once that happens this snippet and its two
  call sites can be deleted outright.

  Images are free Unsplash photos (images.unsplash.com), loaded remotely — the
  same approach the category-grid and instagram-grid sections already use for
  their demo imagery. Unsplash+ premium photos were deliberately excluded.

  Outputs a "|"-delimited list of base image URLs, or nothing if the handle is
  unknown. Callers append their own sizing params.

  @param {string} handle - The product handle to look up

  @example
  {% capture demo %}{% render 'nani-demo-media', handle: product.handle %}{% endcapture %}
  {% assign demo_urls = demo | strip | split: '|' %}
{% enddoc %}

